tOfGrammarReachability%27%2C%20%27definitionsAndProvenanceRetained%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-ONTOLOGY-TAXONOMY-RELATION-DISTINCTION%27%2C%20%27distinction%20between%20general%20relations%20and%20classification%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27The%20ontology%20represents%20concepts%2C%20relationships%20and%20formal%20axioms%3B%20the%20taxonomy%20represents%20classification%20or%20declared%20subsumption.%20An%20arbitrary%20associative%20relation%20does%20not%20become%20a%20classification%20edge%2C%20and%20the%20chosen%20hierarchy%20semantics%20remain%20explicit%20links.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27ontologyAndTaxonomyRolesDistinct%27%2C%20%27arbitraryRelationsDoNotImplyClassification%27%2C%20%27hierarchySemanticsExplicit%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-ONTOLOGY-MULTIPLE-LINK-ROOTS%27%2C%20%27multiple%20explicit%20ontology%20root%20links%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27An%20ontology%20can%20have%20several%20independently%20selectable%20roots%2C%20each%20represented%20as%20an%20explicit%20link%20in%20the%20global%20space.%20A%20root%20may%20also%20be%20a%20type%20only%20when%20its%20model%20declares%20that%20role%3B%20root%20selection%20and%20traversal%20retain%20identity%20and%20provenance.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27multipleOntologyRootsSelectable%27%2C%20%27ontologyRootsAreLinks%27%2C%20%27ontologyRootTypeRoleExplicit%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-TAXONOMY-MULTIPLE-LINK-ROOTS%27%2C%20%27multiple%20explicit%20taxonomy%20root%20links%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27A%20taxonomy%20can%20have%20several%20explicitly%20represented%20root%20links%20and%20multiple%20classification%20entry%20points.%20A%20root%20type%20role%20is%20declared%20by%20the%20selected%20model%20rather%20than%20inferred%20from%20being%20a%20root%2C%20and%20classification%20traversal%20preserves%20its%20declared%20semantics.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27multipleTaxonomyRootsSelectable%27%2C%20%27taxonomyRootsAreLinks%27%2C%20%27taxonomyRootTypeRoleExplicit%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%